hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21047","Bahz and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran, meaning al-Jawni, from Abu Usayb or Abu Usaym, Bahz said: that he attended the prayer over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: how do we pray over him? He said: enter in groups, group after group. He said: so they would enter through this door and pray over him, then exit through the other door. He said: when he was placed in his grave, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Mughirah said: something of his legs remained which they did not fix. They said: then enter and fix it. So he entered and put his hand in and touched his feet, and he said: pile the dust over me. So they piled the dust over him until it reached half his legs, then he came out. And he used to say: I am the most recent of you in contact with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21048","Yazid narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ubayd Abu Nusayrah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Usayb, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me with fever and plague, so I kept fever in Madinah and sent plague to Sham. Plague is martyrdom for my nation and mercy for them, and impurity upon the disbelievers."
"21049","Surayj narrated to us, Hashraj narrated to us, from Abu Nusayrah, from Abu Usayb, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at night and passed by me and called me to him, so I went out. Then he passed by Abu Bakr and called him, so he went out to him. Then he passed by Umar and called him, so he went out to him. Then he went until he entered a garden of one of the Ansar, and he said to the owner of the garden: feed us unripe dates. So he brought a bunch and placed it, and he ate, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions ate. Then he called for cold water and drank, and he said: you will surely be asked about this on the Day of Resurrection. He said: then Umar took the bunch and struck the ground with it until the unripe dates scattered before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said: O Messenger of Allah, are we to be asked about this on the Day of Resurrection? He said: yes, except for three: a rag with which a man covers his nakedness, or a morsel with which he stops his hunger, or a stone he enters into against heat and cold."
